        "ai_gen_block_659cb24_GP3jjk": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_659cb24",
          "name": "FAQ card",
          "settings": {
            "card_title": "サポート・運用定着について",
            "card_subtitle": "導入後の支援、研修、店舗での活用について",
            "icon_type": "users",
            "question_1": "What ongoing maintenance does Flow require?",
            "answer_1": "Flow is designed for low-touch operation. Required maintenance: (1) Camera cleaning: Quarterly (dust/fingerprints affect accuracy). Takes 5 minutes per camera—standard microfiber cloth. (2) Software updates: Automatic, overnight. No downtime. Rollback available if issues detected. (3) Calibration checks: Semi-annual. Flow auto-detects calibration drift and prompts re-calibration (15-minute process per camera). Optional maintenance: (1) Hardware refresh: Cameras rated for 5-year lifespan. Edge units rated for 7 years. (2) Network monitoring: Flow monitors bandwidth usage and alerts if degradation detected. Store staff maintenance: None. System is fully automated. Store managers review alerts and reports, but no daily interaction required unless investigating specific incidents.",
            "question_1_open": false,
            "question_2": "What support and SLAs are included?",
            "answer_2": "Standard support: (1) Business hours: 9 AM - 6 PM JST (Japan), 9 AM - 6 PM local time (other regions). (2) Response time: <4 hours for critical issues, <24 hours for normal inquiries. (3) Channels: Email, web portal, phone (Japan toll-free number). (4) Language: Japanese and English support staff. Premier support (enterprise plan): (1) 24/7 support with <1 hour critical response. (2) Dedicated customer success manager. (3) Quarterly business reviews. (4) Priority feature requests. System SLA: 99.9% uptime (measured monthly). Data accuracy SLA: 98.5% people counting accuracy (measured weekly against manual validation). Compensation: Service credits for SLA breaches (pro-rated based on downtime). Support scope: Includes hardware, software, integrations, and analytics interpretation.",
            "question_2_open": false,
            "question_3": "How is Flow priced and what's included?",
            "answer_3": "Flow uses zone-based subscription pricing. Pricing components: (1) Hardware (one-time): Cameras, edge processing unit, installation. Typical store (10 zones): ¥3-5M JPY one-time. (2) Subscription (annual): Per-zone license covers software, cloud processing, support, updates. Typical store: ¥120-180K JPY/month. Volume discounts for 5+ stores. What's included: Hardware, installation, training, software platform, all analytics features, integrations, standard support, updates. Not included: Network infrastructure upgrades (if required), custom integrations (enterprise feature), on-site staff augmentation. Contract terms: Annual subscription (monthly billing available). 30-day trial at single pilot store (discounted). Multi-year contracts receive pricing lock and priority support. ROI guarantee: If conversion improvement <2% after 6 months, hardware buyback option available.",
            "question_3_open": false,
            "question_4": "What happens if we want to cancel or scale down?",
            "answer_4": "Flow contracts designed for flexibility. Cancellation: 60-day notice required. Annual contract commitment, but can cancel at renewal. If canceling mid-contract, remaining months charged at 50%. Hardware: Customer owns hardware after contract ends—can repurpose cameras for security use or sell back to Flow (depreciated value). Data export: Full data export provided in CSV/JSON format upon cancellation. Data retained 90 days post-cancellation for recovery, then permanently deleted. Scaling down: Reduce zone coverage anytime—subscription adjusts next billing cycle. Seasonal stores: Pause subscription during off-season (e.g., 3-month closure)—resume without re-installation. Migration: If switching to competitor, Flow provides data export and integration support (no lock-in).",
            "question_4_open": false,
